==============================================================================
S5. Is the SUFFIX-side thin band empty for confined words at kappa=0.65?
==============================================================================
  prefix confinement a <= alpha*j forces (e-k)/N >= 1/kappa - (alpha+1)/2 for j=N/2.
   kappa=0.65: (e-k)/N >= +0.245980   > delta=0.1 so suffix band EMPTY
   kappa=0.7: (e-k)/N >= +0.136090   > delta=0.1 so suffix band EMPTY
   kappa=0.8: (e-k)/N >= -0.042481   suffix band may be nonempty
   kappa=0.9: (e-k)/N >= -0.181370   suffix band may be nonempty
  => my 'symmetric extremes' claim was wrong for CONFINED words: the unrestricted
     binomial envelope is symmetric, the confined family is not.  Corrected.
